{
  "case": "due2-max-mixed",
  "source": "Authored for due2; no origin result.",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2 to exercise the max_mixed bound of workflows §6.4. Each of the nine duties is guarded by its own request-source parameter, so W1's conditional-duty hoisting splits each guard g_i into a positive occurrence (the with-duty atom) and a negative one (the without-duty atom): with the parameter missing, every g_i is a mixed variable. Nine unknown guards is k = 9 > max_mixed (8), so the completion falls back to completing the mixed variables independently and records verdict.exact = false. The witness conditions are duty-action refinements with an explicit due2:witnessSource binding (oval-duty-payment, w3c-fs-c1/-c2 use the same form). Scenario 2 sits exactly at the bound (k = 8) and stays exact; scenarios 3–4 have no unknowns. This is the only corpus case whose expected verdict is the fallback's.",
